msgstr "Immediately: wp_mail() reports ‘sent’ only once the provider has accepted the email. Queue: wp_mail() reports ‘sent’ as soon as the email is safely stored. This only means ‘accepted for sending’, not ‘sent’: sending follows in the background, and errors only appear in the log. Emails with very large attachments (over 10 MB) are always sent immediately."

